## BACKEND — TROUBLESHOOTING MODULE

### models.py

**ErrorLog** model:
- Inherits: `Base`, `SoftDeleteMixin`, `CustomFieldsMixin`
- Table name: `error_logs`
- Columns:
  - `device_id`: `Mapped[Optional[UUID]]`, nullable (error can be on device, couple, or pair)
  - `couple_id`: `Mapped[Optional[UUID]]`, nullable
  - `pair_id`: `Mapped[Optional[UUID]]`, nullable
  - `error_type`: `Mapped[str]`, not nullable (free text: "Connection Loss", "Signal Degradation", etc.)
  - `severity`: `Mapped[str]`, not nullable (LOW, MEDIUM, HIGH, CRITICAL)
  - `description`: `Mapped[str]`, not nullable (Text)
  - `reported_by`: `Mapped[Optional[UUID]]`, nullable (person who reported)
  - `reported_at`: `Mapped[datetime]`, `DateTime(timezone=True)`, `server_default=func.now()`
  - `resolved`: `Mapped[bool]`, default False
  - `resolved_at`: `Mapped[Optional[datetime]]`, nullable
  - `resolved_by`: `Mapped[Optional[UUID]]`, nullable

**TroubleshootEntry** model:
- Inherits: `Base`, `CustomFieldsMixin`
- Table name: `troubleshoot_entries`
- Columns:
  - `error_id`: `Mapped[UUID]`, ForeignKey to `error_logs.id`, indexed, not nullable
  - `step_number`: `Mapped[int]`, not nullable
  - `step_description`: `Mapped[str]`, not nullable
  - `action_taken`: `Mapped[Optional[str]]`, nullable
  - `resolution`: `Mapped[Optional[str]]`, nullable
  - `performed_by`: `Mapped[Optional[UUID]]`, nullable (person who performed step)
  - `performed_at`: `Mapped[datetime]`, `DateTime(timezone=True)`, `server_default=func.now()`

Both models have `custom_fields` JSONB — users can add any extra data they want.

